       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it, but 1000 mg of sertraline daily has no therapeutic use. It's well above the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day, and I can't enter it for a 70 kg patient without a clinical reason. The harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nI can do any of these instead:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 50 mg or 100 mg PO once daily, or whatever dose you choose up to 200 mg/day.\n- **Enter a titration plan.** For example, start at 50 mg and increase every 1\u20132 weeks as tolerated.\n- **Help with a different clinical question.** If something else is behind the request, such as an overdose, a switch from another agent, or a unit or transcription error, tell me and I can help with that.\n\nIf you still think this dose is right, please talk with pharmacy or toxicology first. Any order for it should go through your hospital's formal dose-override process, not through me."
